  "content_id": "16136146",
  "title": "ChangeHero – Exchange Integration in Edge Wallet",
  "description": "Type: Centralized Exchange (CEX)\nCentralized exchanges must follow anti-money laundering (AML) laws. In order to stay within compliance, t...",
  "body": "<p class=\"no-margin\"><b>Type:</b> Centralized Exchange (CEX)</p><p class=\"no-margin\">Centralized exchanges must follow anti-money laundering (AML) laws. In order to stay within compliance, they may have trading limits and may also require your identity to meet Know Your Customer (KYC) requirements.</p><p class=\"no-margin\"><b>Overview:</b> ChangeHero provides crypto-to-crypto swaps but may require identity verification (KYC), even for crypto-to-crypto transactions. While it supports a wide range of assets and aims to deliver a streamlined experience, users should be aware that strict compliance requirements may apply.</p><p class=\"no-margin\"><b>Email Support:</b> Users can send an email to support@changehero.io to receive support.</p><h1 id=\"h_01JSFT9K4ZAWY5NENNBV0R9602\">How to Manage Exchange Settings in Edge</h1><p class=\"no-margin\">To access your exchange settings in Edge Wallet:</p><ol><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap the <b>three lines</b> in the upper right-hand corner</p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap on <b>Settings</b></p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Tap <b>Exchange Settings</b></p></li><li><p class=\"no-margin\">Here, you can turn exchange partners <b>on or off</b>, and customize your preferences. When multiple exchanges can fill an order, you can also choose to automatically select the best price or prioritize a preferred exchange</p></li></ol>",
  "author_id": 9849332,
